{"hookSpecificOutput": {"hookEventName": "PreToolUse", "permissionDecision": "deny", "permissionDecisionReason": "dangerous-ops-guard [git-protected-branch]: git reset --hard on a protected branch discards local work on it. Use git stash push then git checkout -B <branch> origin/<branch>, or git reset --keep, or work on a task branch. To reset another repository, use git -C <dir> reset --hard or cd <dir> && git reset --hard. [command-sha256:77b1025165a2d0d932966ebdecc9f9b3ebac406c5d6ecff1ee0adf7147fce375] If you truly intend this, run it in a shell outside the harness, or update harness/hooks/lib/dangerous_ops_guard.py to exempt the pattern."}}
